{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1513472-behold-the-power-of-the-void-nothing-happens","id":1513472,"title":"Behold the power of the Void! [Nothing happens]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-31T15:59:04-07:00","id":1513472,"title":"Behold the power of the Void! [Nothing happens]","content":"So, I've got a weird fixation at the moment on void spirits. I don't mean the spirits from space, but concepts like the number zero, silence, absence, and so on. 1e's Book of Spirits mention void spirits in a sidebar and gives an example in the form of the Hollow Men. I have in mind a group of void spirits calling themselves the Empty Set. They're currently taking up residence in some vacant buildings and one is currently influencing an obsessive artist to make resonant abstract paintings.<br /> <br /> The members I've thought of so far:<ul><li>One Who Names Nothing, Spirit of &quot;zero&quot; and other symbols for nothing (named the group)</li> <li>One Who Is Not Here: Spirit of absence, must immediately leave if anyone (not associated with void) acknowledges its presence (Ban)</li> <li>One Who Lives Nowhere: Has its own Place That Isn't</li> <li>The Unburdened: Spirit of lacking/aestheticism</li> <li>Unnamed Spirit of Silence: To speak its name it is to destroy it (or at least inflict aggravated damage, Bane)</li> </ul>I'm still figuring out what to do with the group, and thought I'd pick the Werewolf community's brains for some inspiration. I'm looking for ideas on:<ul><li>Consequences of spreading their resonance in the mortal world and possible effects of the artist's paintings.</li> <li>Uses of &quot;Void&quot; as an Influence. (Emptying an enemy's ammo or expanding empty spaces comes to mind)</li> <li>Secondary Influences these spirits might have</li> <li>Appropriate Bans and Banes (Mostly Rank 2-3)</li> <li>Any interesting mechanical touches</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T17:00:12-07:00","id":1513481,"title":"","content":"Ooh. An idea for the first one.<br /> <br /> <b>The Countless</b>, a concept-spirit of the number zero and imaginary numbers. Uses <b>Influence: Numbers</b> to get into the heads of mathematicians and have them obsess over impossible equations and theorems.<br /> <b>Ban</b>: Must leave the scene when asked to count the numbers of something.<br /> <b>Bane</b>: Any attack made by its last possible effort; the last arrow in a quiver, the last swing of a cracked sword, the last bullet in a clip, the last punch thrown by someone nearly fainting.<br /> <b>New Numen \u2014 One From Zero</b>: Once per chapter, when depleted of either Willpower or Essence, can instantly refill it to the full by emptying out the other.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<b>Gifts &amp; Fetishes</b>: The Countless can teach the Gift of Evasion, of Knowledge, and the Catastrophe Facet of the Gift of the Elementals. When bound into a fetish, it changes the Sheep\u2019s Clothing feature of the Hishu form to work only when its wielder splits away from a crowd to become alone (sans anyone hot on her trails) \u2014 but in this variation, all mundane efforts to find or chase the wielder fails, with supernatural attempts suffering the usual penalty equal to the wielder\u2019s Primal Urge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T17:42:25-07:00","id":1513486,"title":"","content":"<b>The Absence</b>, a concept-spirit of lost objects and missing people. Uses <b>Influence: <i>Missing</i></b> to inconvenience humans and Uratha alike, from keeping any lost or misplaced items - such as keys, cards, clothing etc. - from being found to actively disrupting search-and-rescue operations and police investigations to keep important evidence, lost pets and children, and human remains concealed and safe from discovery.<br /> <b>Ban: </b><i>Must immediately leave the scene if its presence is directly addressed or acknowledged.</i><br /> <b>Bane: </b><i>Any object taken from a lost-and-found box in the scene, posters and photographs of missing people that have since been rediscovered.</i><br /> <b>New Numen \u2014</b>\u200b <b>Schrodinger's Cat:</b> While successfully concealed during a scene, the Absence can move up to triple its Speed - as per the Speed Numen - for free. If it fails against a contested Perception roll or makes contact with its bane, the benefits of this Numen are deactivated for the duration of the scene.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T08:01:31-07:00","id":1513532,"title":"","content":"New Numen: Existential Lack: The entity straddles the line between existence and non-existence. Beings without Influences in Void, Oblivion, or similar cannot perceive it without a perception roll. Supernatural powers that specifically target the entity automatically suffer a penalty to dice pools equal to its Rank, even if the entity is willing.<br /> <br /> One Who Names Nothing, spirit of &quot;zero&quot; and other symbols for nothing.<br /> Rank 2<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Void 2, Symbols 1<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Fetter, Possess<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Existential Lack, Implant Mission<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must retreat from large crowds.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Symbols for Infinity<br /> One Who Names Nothing has fettered itself to an artist who specializes in abstract art and mathematics, Urging him to depict equally abstract concepts in his paintings. These paintings alter the local resonance to the spirit's liking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}